# What Vercel deploys is decided by vercel.json, and it is two builds:
#
#   * ONE function built from api/server.js (the whole Express app --
#     routes and helpers are bundled into it, not turned into functions of
#     their own, which is what broke the first build against the Hobby
#     plan's limit of 12). /api/* and /auth/* go to it.
#   * the site, the Next.js app in src/, with public/ for the artwork, the
#     fonts and the rules PDF. Everything else goes to it.
#
# The database connection comes from DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED / DATABASE_URL,
# which the Neon integration sets. SESSION_SECRET must be set by hand.
#
# Nothing below is needed at runtime.
api/test
api/scripts
db
qa_frontend.ps1
